        "notes": "SUBSTANTIVE FINDING flagged, not edited: the \"Equivalently\" sentence understates the boxed set. Boxed: NonBaer(H_n(q)) = {q : q^{2k} = 1 for some k in 2..n}. Restated as: \"q is a primitive 2k-th root of unity for some 2 <= k <= n ... q in {zeta_4, zeta_6, zeta_8, ..., zeta_{2n}} (primitive forms only)\". That list omits the ODD-order roots, which the boxed set contains. Counterexample: q = zeta_3 satisfies q^6 = 1, so k = 3 puts it in the boxed set, and directly [3]_{zeta_3} = (zeta_3^3 - zeta_3^{-3})/(zeta_3 - zeta_3^{-1}) = 0/(i sqrt 3) = 0, so H_3(zeta_3) is genuinely non-semisimple - yet zeta_3 is a primitive 3rd root, not a primitive 2k-th root of any order. Correct enumeration: primitive d-th roots with d even and 4 <= d <= 2n, TOGETHER WITH d odd and 3 <= d <= n. Proposed fix: replace the \"Equivalently\" sentence with that two-case statement; the boxed display itself is correct and should stand."
